    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1106">

                <pb facs="0803" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4303.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister at Mexico
                            City to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. I have information from British Minister here that at the suggestion of
                    American Consul at Ensenada, Lower California, some sixty or seventy-five
                    Americans have concentrated at San Quentin and that they are suffering all kinds
                    of hardships due to their lack of means and the difficulty of reaching them to
                    furnish assistance. It seems therefore imperative that a transport be sent there
                    immediately. <pb facs="0804" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/> I have asked the British
                    Minister to instruct his nearest Consul to furnish assistance at our expense,
                    but while he promised to telegraph he fears his Consul may not have the funds to
                    do so, or that available communication may not be at hand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliviera</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
